WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:01.401
Two years ago,

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.202
on January the

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:04.904
sixth, our democracy was attacked.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.374
No other way of saying

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:07.874
the U.S.

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:09.008
Capitol was breached,

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:10.110
which had never happened

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.611
before in the history

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.912
of the United States of America,

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.415
even during the Civil War.

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:17.183
A violent mob of insurrectionists

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:20.720
assaulted law enforcement vendor lives,

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:22.956
sacred halls,

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:25.525
hunted down elected officials,

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:26.726
all for the purpose,

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:27.127
an attempt

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:30.330
to overthrow the will of the people

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:34.100
and usurp the peaceful transfer of power.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.035
All of it,

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:38.738
all of it was fueled

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:41.107
by lies about the 2020 election.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:44.010
But on this day, two years ago,

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:47.547
our democracy held because we the people,

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:49.649
as the Constitution refers

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:52.418
us, we the people did not flinch.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.922
We the people endured.

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:57.857
We the people prevailed.

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.292
And on this day of remembrance,

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:00.260
joined by the vice

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.628
president of the second gentleman

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:03.196
and all of you.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:06.099
We honor a remarkable group of Americans

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.201
who embodied the best

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:10.270
before during and after

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:13.573
January the sixth 2021.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:15.541
For the first time in

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:17.143
my presidency,

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.044
I am bestowing

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:20.213
the presidential citizen's medal.

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:22.081
One of our nation's highest

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:23.983
civilian honors

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.118
recognizes, quote,

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:27.287
citizens of the United States of America

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:28.388
who have performed

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:30.423
exemplary deeds of service

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:31.724
for their country

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.893
or their fellow citizens, end of quote.

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:37.730
In a few moments and a few moments,

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.499
the full citation

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:40.400
of their exemplary

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.669
deeds will be read by military aid.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.138
But this is who these people,

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:46.739
these extraordinary Americans

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:49.809
are heroic law enforcement officers.

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:52.078
As Congressman Bennie Thompson

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.613
said, a man of immense character

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:54.414
and honor himself

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.349
eloquently said about these officers.

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.650
He said, quote,

00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:01.020
You held the line that day.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.588
And what was on the line

00:02:02.588 --> 00:02:04.524
was our democracy.

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:06.592
And history will remember your names

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.163
and history will remember your names,

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:12.231
remember your courage,

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:14.734
remember your bravery, and remember

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.135
your extraordinary commitments

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:17.770
to your fellow Americans.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.238
That's not hyperbole.

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:21.607
That's a fact. That's a fact.

00:02:22.608 --> 00:02:23.609
Folks, history also

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:23.876
going to

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:25.344
remember your instincts

00:02:25.344 --> 00:02:28.114
to respond, to do something as you did.

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:30.483
And as we all watched.

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.718
This is the irony of it all.

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:35.788
All of America watched it, watched it on

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:38.224
television, saw it repeated and repeated.

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.494
In the past months,

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:41.961
we've heard

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:43.796
you testified to the nation

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.832
about what happened that day.

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:46.899
What you were thinking of

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:49.468
at the time was happening,

00:02:49.468 --> 00:02:51.637
what you're thinking now,

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:53.005
the threats,

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:54.540
the violence, the savage

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.342
loss of what happened,

00:02:56.842 --> 00:02:59.212
the trauma all real.

00:03:00.646 --> 00:03:02.315
And it's not exaggeration to say

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:04.350
America owes you,

00:03:04.383 --> 00:03:05.318
owes you all.

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:07.019
I really mean this

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:09.155
debt a debt of gratitude

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:12.458
when we can never fully repay

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:14.493
unless we live up to what you did,

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:18.130
live up to what you did.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:20.700
And what you did was truly consequential

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:22.268
and a joke.

00:03:23.502 --> 00:03:24.437
If I can hold for

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:27.540
a second and just say to you,

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.010
the impact, what happened on July

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.845
six had international repercussions

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:33.713
beyond what I think

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:36.782
any of you can fully understand.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:39.118
The first meeting I had of what they call

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:41.587
the G-7, the seven leading

00:03:42.154 --> 00:03:44.857
economies in the world, democracies.

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:47.660
I sat down was in February.

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:49.128
I was in England,

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:51.664
and I sat next to the president

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:52.698
of France, across

00:03:52.698 --> 00:03:54.934
from the chancellor, from Germany, etc.

00:03:56.068 --> 00:03:59.071
And I said, America's back.

00:03:59.071 --> 00:04:01.774
Know what the response was as a joke?

00:04:02.441 --> 00:04:04.210
For how long

00:04:05.277 --> 00:04:07.713
for how long

00:04:09.548 --> 00:04:12.284
And I just sat there and looked

00:04:12.284 --> 00:04:12.852
and I believe

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:14.019
it was the prime minister of Italy.

00:04:14.019 --> 00:04:14.353
He said,

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:15.788
but I can't remember for certain

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:18.724
which of the 76 said it

00:04:18.724 --> 00:04:20.192
What would you think, Mr. President,

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.962
if tomorrow

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:24.130
you woke up and

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.332
you have a headline in the press

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:28.534
saying that in the British Parliament,

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.035
a mob

00:04:30.402 --> 00:04:32.404
had come down the hall, broken down

00:04:32.404 --> 00:04:35.474
the doors of the House of Commons,

00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:37.776
police officers were killed or died

00:04:40.145 --> 00:04:43.015
the place was vandalized

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:45.851
in order to overthrow the election

00:04:45.851 --> 00:04:48.153
of the Speaker of the House.

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:52.992
A Prime Minister's election

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:55.661
Think about it.

00:04:56.962 --> 00:04:58.230
Think about it

00:04:58.964 --> 00:05:01.000
or we think if we heard that news today,

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:02.434
any other

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:04.136
the leading democracy in the world

00:05:04.136 --> 00:05:05.404
through this,

00:05:06.071 --> 00:05:07.406
some folks

00:05:08.507 --> 00:05:09.808
these people and the people

00:05:09.808 --> 00:05:10.643
representing those

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:11.510
who couldn't be here

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:15.114
because they gave their lives for this

00:05:15.247 --> 00:05:17.950
did is incredibly consequential.

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:20.886
It's just that's not political talk.

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:23.288
That's a historical fact.

00:05:23.288 --> 00:05:24.189
Folks,

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:27.426
I fellow Americans,

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:30.029
I want you to give one round of applause.

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:31.563
Again, today's recipients

00:05:31.563 --> 00:05:32.931
of the Presidential Citizen's

00:05:32.931 --> 00:05:33.832
Medal Patriots

00:05:33.832 --> 00:05:34.666
who have performed

00:05:34.666 --> 00:05:35.701
exemplary deeds

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:38.203
in the service of this great nation.

00:05:38.203 --> 00:05:39.972
Let me close with this.

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:43.642
82 years ago, on this very day in 1941,

00:05:44.576 --> 00:05:45.577
President Franklin

00:05:45.577 --> 00:05:46.678
Roosevelt delivered his

00:05:46.678 --> 00:05:47.980
State of the Union address

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:50.349
that became known

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:52.518
as his famous for freedom speech

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:54.820
as he defined America's

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.655
place in the world.

00:05:56.655 --> 00:05:58.056
He reminded

00:05:58.056 --> 00:05:58.991
the American people

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:00.659
